/*
 * words.es.js — Daily Murder Sudoku, full Spanish (Español) dictionary.
 *
 * Grammar strategy (no agreement across #N slots — see the renderer):
 *   - Rooms, terrain and roles fold their own definite article into the
 *     entry ("la cocina", "la hierba", "el guardia"); 546/547 stay the bare,
 *     contraction-free "en #1" / "sobre #1".
 *   - Singular trait/person nouns fold an indefinite article in ("una mujer",
 *     "una persona con gafas"); plural forms stay bare ("mujeres"). Object
 *     nouns fold an indefinite article in too; 534/535 collapse onto the
 *     same indefinite passthrough (escape hatch: "a piano" stays true even
 *     when there is only one).
 *   - Every predicate fragment (500s) carries its own verb ("estaba …" /
 *     "no estaba …"), so template 400 is a bare "#1 #2." — the only way to
 *     get Spanish's pre-verb "no" right without cross-slot agreement.
 *   - "a"/"de" are avoided wherever a slot filler could start with "el":
 *     "justo contra" replaces "junto a" for beside/next-to, and "que" for
 *     comparisons replaces "de" after a direction ("más al norte que #1").
 *   - Gendered participles that would have to agree with an unknown-gender
 *     subject are dodged with invariant wording instead: "a solas" (never
 *     "solo/sola") for alone, "en posición sentada/tumbada" (agreeing with
 *     "posición", not the subject) for postures.
 */
